# Exemptions for .githooks/leak-guard.sh.
#
# One entry per line:
#
#     <path>:<literal><TAB><why it is safe>
#
# The path is repo-relative, the literal is the exact text the guard reported. Never a line
# number: line numbers drift, the literal does not. The reason is required and lives on the
# entry's own line -- an earlier design read it from the comment above and this file's own
# header silently counted as the reason for the first entry.
#
# This file starts empty and should stay that way. An entry here is an owner decision made per
# line, not a way to turn a red scan green. The LICENSE needs no entry: the GitHub handle is not
# one of the patterns.
